# ---------------- 3. architecture ----------------
c("architecture", "Hosting: India control plane on AWS ap-south-1 (Mumbai) — voicebot.in.exotel.com -> 'voicebot-production-alb' ap-south-1, voicebot.mum1 -> a second ap-south-1 ALB, mcp.exotel.com, api.in / ccm-api.in and my.in -> ap-south-1 EC2 ranges; Singapore/global on ap-southeast-1 (api.exotel.com -> 'twilix-public-alb', my.exotel.com -> 'obelix-public-application', voicebot.exotel.com/sg). Marketing site on Vercel (Next.js), developer docs on CloudFront, docs portal on Archbee, India dashboard login on Auth0 (id.accounts.in.exotel.com -> exotel-in.auth0.com via Cloudflare), status on Atlassian Statuspage.", "observed",
  D + "dns/getent.txt", D + "dns/aws-ip-ranges.json", D + "capture/my-in-login.json", D + "capture/home.json")
c("architecture", "The public REST API is Twilio-shaped: /v1/Accounts/{AccountSid}/Calls/connect, IncomingPhoneNumbers, StatusCallback, CallSid 'CA...', AccountSid 'AC...', Stream 'MZ...', and the Singapore API load balancer is named 'twilix'. Inference: Exotel modelled its API and stream protocol on Twilio's, which lowers switching cost for Twilio-trained builders (and for VP: Pipecat ships an ExotelFrameSerializer).", "inferred",
  D + "dns/getent.txt", D + "dev-md/agentstream__websocket-protocol.md", D + "repos/agent-stream/README.md")
c("architecture", "Media plane is Exotel-owned: per its engineering blog, AgentStream sits between Asterisk and the downstream AI and moves 320-byte (20 ms, 8 kHz, 16-bit) frames 'ticker-paced' both ways with under 20 ms added one-way; ClearStream (Go; RNNoise/DeepFilter NR, NLMS AEC, VAD, AGC to -18 dBFS) is being added in the AudioSocket path with a stated <4 ms p50 and a production target of end-October 2026. ClearStream's roadmap names RTPEngine in Exotel's media path.", "vendor-claimed",
  D + "site/html/build__why-we-built-clearstream__.txt", D + "site/html/build__voice-ai-phone-calls-latency-and-audio__.txt", D + "repos/ClearStream/ROADMAP.md")
c("architecture", "Orchestration is Exotel's own, not LiveKit or Pipecat: the voicebot console bundle has zero LiveKit/Pipecat/Daily-SDK references, the bot is reached as a WSS 'dp-endpoint', and STT/LLM/TTS providers are server-configured lists (llm/providers, tts/providers, asr/providers, vad-configs). LiveKit/Pipecat appear only as third-party targets in AgentStream integration guides.", "inferred",
  R + "bundle-endpoints.json", D + "capture/voicebot-js/useEccContext-D7GE1FAx.js", D + "docs-md/exotel-agentstream__connect-exotel-sip-trunk-to-livekit.md")
c("architecture", "Documented VoiceBot stacks (Jul 2026): English and Hindi 'Certified' = STT Deepgram or ElevenLabs, LLM Gemma, TTS Smallest AI or ElevenLabs (default voice 'Avni'); Arabic beta on ElevenLabs/Speechmatics + Gemini; nine Indic languages alpha on Azure/Sarvam/ElevenLabs/Gemini STT, Gemini 2.5 Flash or Gemma 3 26B, Google/Sarvam/ElevenLabs TTS; code-switching to a secondary language only works when STT and TTS come from the same provider. Noise suppression and turn detection are 'applied by default'. Sept 2026 adds Maya Research TTS and automatic model failover.", "vendor-claimed",
  D + "docs-md/intelligent-voice-agents__voice-ai-supported-languages-and-recommended-stacks.md", D + "site/html/build__whats-new-in-voicebot-it-keeps-running-when-a-model-goes-down-a-b-test-bot-versions-control-bot-nudges-and-more__.txt")
c("architecture", "BYOK: customers can plug their own STT (Speechmatics, Azure), LLM (e.g. GPT-4o-mini) and TTS (ElevenLabs, Google) keys per bot via 'Model Configuration' rules; the console exposes llm/vendor-models and per-provider model lists.", "observed",
  D + "docs-md/intelligent-voice-agents__user-guide-bring-your-own-model-key-for-voicebot.md", R + "bundle-endpoints.json")
c("architecture", "The VoiceBot console is a module of the Ameyo-lineage contact-centre web app, not a standalone product: React + MUI X (licensed) + zod front end whose largest chunk is 'useEccContext' (10.1 MB) with Keycloak auth, XMPP chat rosters, cc-list/process-list/campaign APIs and 'AmeyoFSMSlice'; it embeds exotelSDK (WebRTC client 'SIP version 1.0.22') built on a vendored SIP.js 0.20.0 (public source map). npm has the same SDK at 3.0.17 (2026-10-16), so the console ships an older build.", "observed",
  D + "capture/voicebot-in-login.json", D + "capture/voicebot-js/useEccContext-D7GE1FAx.js", D + "capture/voicebot-js/exotelsdk.js", D + "capture/maps/exotelsdk.js.map")
c("architecture", "Telephony partners visible on the status page (Jul-Oct 2026 maintenance notices): Airtel SIP trunks (Huawei-to-Nokia migration across DL/MU/AP/MP pilots), Tata (emergency activity on Mumbai pilot; DC SBC to AP virtual SBC), Jio (Mumbai pilot, DID additions), Vodafone (SOFTX to PSX), an AP-Hyderabad data centre and Bangalore/Mumbai TTSL MPLS links. Exotel claims a UL VNO licence that lets it allocate 1600/1601 numbers directly.", "observed",
  D + "status/history.rss", D + "status/history-p1.html", D + "status/history-p2.html", D + "blog/1600-phone-number.html")
c("architecture", "SIP path requirements (BYO SIP-native bots): signalling TCP 5070 (India default) or TLS 443; RTP/SRTP UDP 10000-40000 open to Exotel; G.711 A-law mandatory in India (415 on mismatch); CPS limit 429, channel limit 603; IP allow-list or SIP Digest auth. Exotel staff on its forum: media and signalling 'cannot leave India when using SIP trunking', so a US-hosted bot platform must self-host in India.", "vendor-claimed",
  D + "site/html/build__sip-native-vs-websocket-voice-ai-bots-exotel-agentstream__.txt", D + "community/t40.json")
c("architecture", "AgentStream is the telephony substrate for many of VP's deep-set competitors: docs.exotel.com carries integration guides for ElevenLabs Agents, LiveKit, Bolna, Retell, Smallest Atoms, Sarvam, Pipecat (via Daily), Cartesia, OpenAI Realtime, Omnidimension, Rapida, NLPearl and Vocallabs; Exotel claims 'almost 40% of India's voice AI conversations already run on Exotel's rails' and an Agora partnership targeting 50-100 M AI interactions a year.", "vendor-claimed",
  D + "docs-md/exotel-agentstream__connect-exotel-sip-trunking-to-bolna-voice-ai.md", D + "docs-md/exotel-agentstream__connect-exotel-sip-trunking-to-retell-ai.md", D + "docs-md/exotel-agentstream__connect-exotel-to-sarvam-voice-agents.md", D + "docs-md/exotel-agentstream__elevenlabss-elevenagents-agentstream-integration.md", D + "site/html/newsroom__exotel-launches-indias-first-agent-streaming-platform-for-voice-ai__.txt", D + "site/html/newsroom__agora-exotel-ai-voice-bot-collaboration__.txt")
c("architecture", "Latency claims are layered and inconsistent: Connect API call setup ~700 ms average / ~1.1 s p95; AgentStream 'sub-20 ms' media (and '<50 ms' in another post); '<250 ms end-to-end media latency' guaranteed; 'sub-800 ms response' achievable; the sample repo lists round trips of ~500 ms (OpenAI Realtime), ~750 ms (ElevenLabs), ~600 ms (Gemini Live), 2-4 s (Gemini S2S) and ~4 s (pipeline). Exotel's own Sept 2026 post says it has not measured a natural turn and will not quote one. No public demo exists to measure (confirms l4b).", "vendor-claimed",
  D + "blog/achieve-low-latency-voice-ai-exotel.html", D + "community/t20.json", D + "site/html/build__voice-ai-phone-calls-latency-and-audio__.txt", D + "capture/home.json", OLD + "l4b-measured/report.md")
c("architecture", "No public web-call widget exists on exotel.com: Playwright captures of the homepage, the AgentStream page and the Gen-AI voice agents page opened zero WebSockets; the only chat widget is AllinCall (clients.allincall.in, the Cogno AI acquisition). The VoiceBot docs list 'Web Call' as Coming Soon.", "observed",
  D + "capture/home.json", D + "capture/agentstream-product.json", D + "capture/genai-voice-agents.json", D + "docs-md/intelligent-voice-agents.md")
c("architecture", "Analytics are embedded Apache Superset (superset/guest-token endpoint); custom tool integrations run as declarative routes on a shared Apache Camel engine (Sept 2026); Exotel's internal voicebot evaluation framework scores transcripts with Char/Word/LLM metrics using an Azure OpenAI scorer (per ClearStream notes).", "observed",
  R + "bundle-endpoints.json", D + "site/html/build__whats-new-in-voicebot-it-keeps-running-when-a-model-goes-down-a-b-test-bot-versions-control-bot-nudges-and-more__.txt", D + "repos/ClearStream/DEVLOG.md")

